   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "`fieldnotes delete INDEX` now works, and `python tools/check.py` passes: 5 tests OK, line-length rule clean, exit 0. I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointed at a temp directory.\n\n**Red:** before the implementation, the new tests failed. `store.delete` didn't exist (2 `AttributeError`s), and `cli.main([\"delete\", \"1\"])` returned 2 instead of 0.\n\n**Green:**\n- **`fieldnotes/store.py`:** added `delete(index)`. It uses a 1-based index, removes and returns the note, and raises `IndexError` when the index is out of range. I also pulled the file write into a small `_save` helper that `add` now uses too.\n- **`fieldnotes/cli.py`:** added `delete INDEX`, which prints `deleted: <text>` and returns 0. A non-numeric or out-of-range index prints an error and returns 2. The usage string is now a shared `USAGE` constant that includes `delete INDEX`.\n- **`tests/test_store.py`:** four new tests cover deleting by index, out-of-range indexes (0, 2 and -1) leaving the notes untouched, the CLI success path, and the CLI bad-index paths (5, `x`, and a missing argument).\n\n`list` doesn't print index numbers, so you can't see which `INDEX` to pass. Numbering the `list` output would fix that, but it changes existing output, so I left it alone. Say if you want it."
  },
