   "reply": "I added a `count` command that prints how many notes there are. `python tools/check.py` passes: all 7 tests pass, there are no line-length violations, and it exits 0.\n\n- **Command:** `fieldnotes/cli.py` now handles `count` and prints `len(store.load())`. I also added `count` to the usage string.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_store.py` has a new `CliCountTests` class. One test checks that an empty store prints `0`, and the other checks that two added notes print `2`.\n- **Environment:** `check.py` needs `NOTES_HOME`, which wasn't set in this shell. I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` pointing at a fresh temp directory, so nothing was written inside the project.\n\nThe error and usage lines in the check output come from the existing `delete` bad-index test."
